## Structural Skeleton (to be replaced by real Nougat MMD output)

## Abstract

Radiation-induced skin toxicity is a dose-limiting side effect of radiotherapy. The authors use an N/TERT-1 3D organotypic skin model exposed to 2 Gy low-LET X-rays to characterize NF-$\kappa$B activation, COX-2 induction, PGE\textsubscript{2} release, and downstream perturbation of keratinocyte terminal differentiation (K1, filaggrin, cornified-layer thickness).

## 1. Introduction

Skin is the first tissue exposed in radiotherapy; radiation-induced skin toxicity ranges from erythema to moist desquamation to fibrosis. NF-$\kappa$B is a canonical redox-sensitive transcription factor activated by ionizing radiation via IKK$\beta$; downstream targets include the inducible cyclooxygenase COX-2 (PTGS2). COX-2 produces prostaglandin E\textsubscript{2} (PGE\textsubscript{2}), a lipid mediator with pro-inflammatory and cell-fate-modulating activity.

## 2. Materials and Methods

### 2.1 Cell culture
N/TERT-1 immortalized keratinocytes cultured as 3D organotypic skin equivalents on collagen-fibroblast rafts.

### 2.2 Irradiation
2 Gy X-rays, single-fraction, room temperature.

### 2.3 Pharmacology
- sc-236 (COX-2 inhibitor, working dose 5 $\mu$M)
- Bay 11-7085 (NF-$\kappa$B inhibitor, working dose 1 $\mu$M)

### 2.4 qRT-PCR
$2^{-\Delta\Delta C_T}$ method (Livak & Schmittgen 2001):

$$
\Delta C_T^{\text{test}} = C_T^{\text{target,test}} - C_T^{\text{ref,test}}
$$

$$
\Delta C_T^{\text{calib}} = C_T^{\text{target,calib}} - C_T^{\text{ref,calib}}
$$

$$
\Delta\Delta C_T = \Delta C_T^{\text{test}} - \Delta C_T^{\text{calib}}
$$

$$
\text{ratio} = 2^{-\Delta\Delta C_T}
$$

### 2.5 Western blot
p-p65 (Ser536), p-p38, COX-2. Densitometry by ImageJ.

### 2.6 Immunohistochemistry
K1 and filaggrin (FLG) by immunofluorescence; cornified-layer thickness by H\&E morphometry.

### 2.7 MTT viability
5-dose-point response for sc-236 and Bay 11-7085.

### 2.8 PGE\textsubscript{2} ELISA
Culture-supernatant PGE\textsubscript{2} quantification by commercial ELISA.

### 2.9 Statistics
One-way ANOVA + Tukey HSD. n=2 or n=3 per group as noted per figure.

## 3. Results (figures)

- **Fig 1.** COX-2 mRNA timecourse, control + irradiated arms with sc-236 rescue.
- **Fig 2.** MTT dose-response for sc-236 (2A) and Bay 11-7085 (2B).
- **Fig 3.** K1 (3B/3C) and FLG (3D/3E) immunofluorescence with sc-236 perturbation.
- **Fig 4.** p-p65 and p-p38 Western blots (4A) + densitometry (4B).
- **Fig 5.** COX-2 (5A/5B) and p-p65 (5C) dose ladders with Bay 11-7085.
- **Fig 6.** Cornified-layer thickness (6D) + K1 (6E) + FLG (6F) with Bay 11-7085 perturbation.
- **Fig 7.** PGE\textsubscript{2} ELISA timecourse (7A) + sc-236 rescue at 72 h (7B).

## 4. Discussion

Authors argue for a linear cascade NF-$\kappa$B $\to$ COX-2 $\to$ PGE\textsubscript{2} $\to$ differentiation disruption, with sc-236 rescuing downstream and Bay 11-7085 suppressing upstream.

## 5. References

Standard bibliography. Frontiers article page hosts the supplementary material (Figure S1 = qPCR calibration curve only). No deposited primary datasets.

